+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+Benchmark: `muninn-bench perf`, full `UserPromptSubmit` hook (intent gate passes,
+i.e. the complete read path runs: term selection → BM25 → filter → budget →
+blocks), measured against the adversarial synthetic store built in
+`crates/muninn-bench/src/main.rs` — a Zipf-distributed vocabulary of 30 frequent
+domain words plus rare identifiers (see `word()`/`WORDS` in that file), chosen
+so posting lists look like real code discussion rather than a corpus where
+every record contains every term.
+
+- **Before the term-selection fix:** full-hook p95 **10.27 ms**.
+- **The fix:** `select_terms()` in `crates/muninn-core/src/recall.rs` now drops
+  candidate terms whose document frequency exceeds a third of the store
+  (`df > n / 3`, gated on `n >= 50`) before ranking the rest by IDF. On the
+  30-word adversarial vocabulary, several of those 30 frequent words appear in
+  most records, so without this cutoff they dominated term selection and each
+  produced a long FTS5 posting list to score.
+- **After the fix:** full-hook p95 **1.82 ms**.
+
+These two numbers come from a prior measurement session on this project (not
+re-measured in this session); no other file in the repository records them
+verbatim, so treat them as reported rather than independently reproduced here.
